# q12-title-hover.script — Q12 event-parity fixture: title-state hover/click
#
# D16 rows exercised (see test/harness/d16-state-machine.md):
#   - MouseMove over the Options button: pressed face while hovering,
#     raised face otherwise (title MotionNotify hover path).
#   - MouseDown/MouseUp on the button: press latch (buttonActivated),
#     release inside -> options.RealizeWindow() + ReleaseButton.
#     NOTE for the X11 leg: the click session blocks inside pollEvents, so
#     the pressed-face draw lands when the drain returns (post-release);
#     capture AFTER release+settle, never between down and up.
#   - pointerButtonReleased gating: keys are ignored until a Button1
#     release has been seen; after the release below, 'h' must work again.
#
# Coordinates: the Options button sits at client (2,2), roughly 60x30
# ("Options" in the button font + borders). On-button point ~(20,15),
# off-button point (360,300). Verify empirically before first run.
#
# Pass criteria (Q12): identical face state at checkpoints across backends;
# key gating state identical (the trailing 'h' produces the help screen).
#
# Run:
#   ./obj/harness --seed 12345 --script test/harness/scripts/q12-title-hover.script \
#       --out DIR --hiscore test/harness/fixtures/hiScore.nul.data

1    capture q12_title0

10   move 20 15               # hover onto the button
30   capture q12_hover_on     # pressed face
50   move 360 300             # hover off
70   capture q12_hover_off    # raised face

90   mousedown 20 15          # press on button
110  mouseup 20 15            # release on button -> RealizeWindow path
140  capture q12_clicked      # face raised again; menu may be realized

160  keydown h                # pointerButtonReleased is on again: works
164  keyup h
190  capture q12_help_after   # help screen proves the gate reopened
